* Fixed Linux disk encryption key escrow rejecting a valid passphrase with "Passphrase incorrect" on hosts whose shell startup files print to stdout: fleetd read the passphrase from the entry dialog's stdout while launching it through the login user's shell, so whatever that shell printed was captured as part of the passphrase. The end-user dialogs now launch without a login shell and inherit the desktop session's environment directly, so they also pick up its locale and input method.
